  <h1>Who built it</h1>

  <p class="lede">Benjamin Hetrick — an infrastructure and incident-response operator who brought change-control discipline to machine learning.</p>

  <p>
    I've spent about fifteen years in enterprise infrastructure and operations, working incident
    response at the L3 level. GameBoyGhost is me applying that discipline — change windows,
    audit trails, sign-offs, blameless postmortems — to a field where it's under-practiced:
    machine learning.
  </p>

  <p>
    I am not an ML researcher, and this project doesn't claim to be one. I'm an operator who wanted
    something concrete to show that I understand how to build, run, evaluate, and — most importantly
    — <em>keep honest</em> an AI system. The game is the flavoring. The infrastructure is the point.
  </p>

  <p>
    The thing I'm most proud of here isn't a milestone. It's that the failures are on the record,
    root-caused, and fixed — and the bar for what counts as "done" got <em>stricter</em> as the work
    went on.
  </p>

